# 10. Methods recap

- Removed exact duplicate rows; recoded `-99` sentinel values to `NA`, including
  free/reduced lunch shares recorded above 1 (logically impossible for a
  proportion).
- Dropped records missing any analysis variable
  (`r format(n_dropped, big.mark = ",")` records, `r pct_dropped`% of the total);
  attrition by year is reported in Section 2.
- Grouped county-years into Low / Medium / High poverty by **tertiles** of the
  county poverty rate. Tertiles were chosen over fixed policy thresholds so the
  three groups hold comparable numbers of observations, keeping group means
  stable. The trade-off is that the cut points are specific to this dataset and
  not comparable across studies.
- Standardized math and ELA scale scores **within each year** so performance is
  comparable across years despite changes in the test instrument.
- Merged school data with ACS county data on `county_name + year` using a **left
  join**, keeping all school records and attaching county context where available.
- Interaction terms in Section 6 were **mean-centered** before multiplication so
  the main effects remain interpretable at the sample average rather than at
  values (such as zero poverty) that do not occur in the data.

